---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import ProductCapture from "../components/ProductCapture.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Features"
  active="/features/"
  description="Explore AtlasOS desktop, education workflows, diagnostics, and its custom UEFI boot frontend."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The Atlas experience"
    title="A Linux environment shaped around the lesson."
    text="AtlasOS brings classroom-oriented navigation and system controls to familiar Linux foundations. The project is actively developing, and each capability has a clearly documented scope."
  />
  <section class="page-content feature-story">
    <div class="shell">
      <article class="feature-story-row">
        <div class="feature-story-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">01 · Before class begins</span>
          <h2>A clear starting point for the day.</h2>
          <p>The Atlas desktop places teaching shortcuts and device status in view, while leaving the wider Linux environment available.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/AtlasOS/screenshots/">View the actual desktop capture →</a>
        </div>
        <ProductCapture
          src="/AtlasOS/images/atlasos-live-desktop.jpeg"
          alt="AtlasOS Live desktop with classroom navigation, resources, lesson tools, and system status"
          title="AtlasOS Live desktop"
          caption="A real capture from the current AtlasOS system."
          kind="desktop"
        />
      </article>
      <article class="feature-story-row feature-story-row-reverse">
        <div class="feature-story-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">02 · A distinct boot identity</span>
          <h2>An Atlas welcome before Linux starts.</h2>
          <p>The Rust UEFI frontend presents AtlasOS boot choices and starts the documented backend in the normal validated path.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/AtlasOS/screenshots/">View the actual boot capture →</a>
        </div>
        <ProductCapture
          src="/AtlasOS/images/atlasos-boot-manager.png"
          alt="AtlasOS boot menu showing Live, Advanced Options, Start from Disk, and System Tools"
          title="Atlas Boot Manager"
          caption="A real boot-menu capture. Firmware appearance can vary by device."
          kind="boot"
        />
      </article>
      <div class="feature-boundary">
        <span class="eyebrow">Designed for evaluation</span>
        <p>AtlasOS currently provides a USB-bootable Live environment. It does not include an installer or an in-place upgrade path. Hardware support remains under evaluation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
